/-!
# Surjectivity of `𝒪_Y ⟶ f_* 𝒪_X` is preserved by every base change

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a proper morphism of schemes all of whose fibres have dimension at most one
and vanishing first structure-sheaf cohomology, and suppose `𝒪_Y ⟶ f_* 𝒪_X` is surjective.
[Stacks, Tag 0E7I] asserts that `𝒪_{Y'} ⟶ f'_* 𝒪_{X'}` is surjective for every base change
`f'` of `f`.

This file carries out the source's own proof, whose shape is a reduction to two cases over an
affine base. Surjectivity is local on the base, so one may work over an affine open `W ⊆ Y`
and an affine open `V ⊆ Y'` mapping into it; the restricted base change is then a base change
of `f ∣_ W` along a morphism of affine schemes. Such a morphism factors as a closed immersion
followed by a flat morphism, through the spectrum of a polynomial algebra on the elements of
the target ring. The flat half is flat base change, [Stacks, Tag 02KH]; the closed-immersion
half is the ideal-sheaf short exact sequence, where the obstruction in the long exact sequence
is killed by clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0E7H].

## Main results

All in the namespace `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange`.

* `epi_unitToPushforwardUnit_of_baseChange`: **[Stacks, Tag 0E7I]**, under exactly the
  hypotheses of the tag. Clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0E7H] enters as the theorem
  `isZero_cohomology_one_of_generatingSections_of_isAffine`, applied over the affine base of the
  closed-immersion half to the ideal sheaf `ℐ 𝒪_X`, never to `𝒪_X` itself.

The degree-zero base-change clause `DirectImageStructureSheafCommutesBaseChangeOfFibreDimensionOne`
of `StructureSheafSurjectivityBaseChange.lean`, whose surjectivity half is equivalent to this
conclusion, is not assumed here.

## Implementation notes

Surjectivity of `𝒪_Y ⟶ f_* 𝒪_X` is `Epi` in the abelian category `Y.Modules` of sheaves of
`𝒪_Y`-modules, which is local surjectivity; this is the spelling the rest of this directory
uses. `Epi` of the same comparison read in sheaves of *rings* would be strictly weaker — the
ring epimorphism `ℤ ⟶ ℚ` is not locally surjective — so the module spelling is the faithful
one, and `Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective` of `Scheme.Hom.toRingCatSheafHom` is used as the
intermediate form through which sections over affine opens are reached.

Over an affine open the comparison reads on sections as `Scheme.Hom.app`, and quasi-coherence
of `f_* 𝒪_X` — [Stacks, Tag 01XJ] in degree zero — turns local surjectivity into surjectivity
of `Γ(Y, W) ⟶ Γ(X, f⁻¹W)`. In the flat half, flat base change identifies global functions
upstairs only as a *cyclic* module over the new base; a commutative ring which is cyclic as a
module over a subring is generated by that subring, which is what turns the identification into
surjectivity of the comparison ring map.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02KH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01JU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01JU)
-/

